<PageLayout title="Editorial Policy" description="Our source standards, fact-checking process, update schedule, corrections policy and how we use AI tools when researching cases." updated="2026-11-01">
  <h2>Source standards</h2>
  <p>We prefer primary sources: founders' own posts and interviews, company pages and reputable media. Every case lists its sources, and every source link is checked before publishing.</p>
  <h2>Fact-checking</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Each number is stored with its source link, source date and a provenance label: founder-reported, verified, media-reported or unverified (a quoted figure we could not confirm against its original source).</li>
    <li>Figures without a reliable source are marked "Not disclosed", never estimated.</li>
  </ol>
  <h2>Use of AI</h2>
  <p>We use AI tools to help draft text and code. AI is a drafting aid, not a source: no number is published because an AI produced it. Content is reviewed for accuracy and usefulness before publishing, following Google's guidance on helpful, people-first content.</p>
  <h2>Helpful content checklist</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Who</strong> made it? Pages name the Editorial team and link to its page.</li>
    <li><strong>How</strong> was it made? Pages show sources, worked examples and the date they were last updated.</li>
    <li><strong>Why</strong> does it exist? To answer a real question or do a real job, not to fill search results. We do not publish cases we cannot source.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Updates</h2>
  <p>We re-check case figures when new sources appear. We review each page at least every 90 days. The "Last updated" date only changes when content changes in substance.</p>
  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>To report an error, see the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. Confirmed errors are fixed promptly and the page's date is updated.</p>
  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>The site currently shows no ads. If ads are added later, they will be clearly labelled and will never influence content.</p>
</PageLayout>
